From d0a1bcd09033abb0315f4d98169dde78060797d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Unbundle grpc

Replace the grpc module from the BCR with the stub in
third_party/systemlibs/grpc (installed by build.sh from recipe/systemlibs).

Bazel never builds gRPC from source: third_party/grpc/BUILD links conda's
libgrpc, and the Starlark rules it needs are vendored in
third_party/grpc/bazel. The BCR module is only there to satisfy the bazel_dep
-- but its MODULE.bazel calls register_toolchains, which forces its root
package to load, and grpc's BUILD files load
@com_google_protobuf//bazel:upb_proto_reflection_library.bzl, which protobuf
ships as a shim forwarding to //upb/bazel -- a package our protobuf systemlib
does not have:

    ERROR: ... invalid registered toolchain
    '//:python_3_11_ios_sim_arm64_workaround': error loading package '@@grpc+//':
    ... Label '@@protobuf+//upb/bazel:upb_proto_reflection_library.bzl' is
    invalid because 'upb/bazel' is not a package

The grpc-java module is left on the BCR: its Java artifacts are really used,
and it does not drag in grpc's BUILD files.

This mirrors what the main branch does for 9.x.
---
 MODULE.bazel | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MODULE.bazel b/MODULE.bazel
index 42f384e5a5..3b7a5c1f00 100644
--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -50,6 +50,12 @@ local_path_override(
     path = "./third_party/systemlibs/protobuf",
 )
 
+# See third_party/systemlibs/grpc/MODULE.bazel for why the BCR module is replaced.
+local_path_override(
+    module_name = "grpc",
+    path = "./third_party/systemlibs/grpc",
+)
+
 # TODO: wyv@ - add remoteapis to the BCR
 bazel_dep(name = "remoteapis", version = "")
 
